The Iron Man Mark XLIII (43) suit serves as Tony Stark’s primary battle armor at the start of Avengers: Age of Ultron, taking the revolutionary autonomous prehensile tech introduced in the Mark 42 and turning it into a battle-hardened, reliable military machine. Cosmetically, it flips the Mark 42's color palette back to a classic dark hot-rod red dominance with subtle gold trim, while under the hood it features reinforced plating, upgraded repulsors, shoulder-mounted micro-missiles, an improved internal HUD, and a specialized infrared scanning mode used to locate Hydra targets inside the Sokovian fortress. Beyond its standalone combat effectiveness, the Mark 43 was engineered as the core baseline suit designed to interface directly with the Veronica orbital deployment system, allowing Tony to call down and dock inside the massive Hulkbuster armor whenever Bruce Banner lost control.
